    "title": "Accessibility statement",
    "intro": "We believe everyone should be able to enjoy our venue and our website comfortably and independently. Here is what we have done, and how to reach us.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Our commitment to accessibility",
        "body": [
          "Baloona is committed to serving all of our guests equally and to improving the service we give guests with disabilities. We invest significant effort and resources in making both the website and the venue accessible, in the belief that everyone deserves equality, dignity, comfort and independence."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Website accessibility",
        "body": [
          "This website was made accessible in line with the Israeli Equal Rights for Persons with Disabilities Regulations (Service Accessibility Adjustments), 2013, and the Israeli standard (IS 5568) based on WCAG 2.1 level AA.",
          "The site is built for the common browsers and for mobile use, and supports keyboard navigation and screen readers."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Accessibility features on the site",
        "list": [
          "Valid semantic structure that assistive technologies can navigate.",
          "Sufficient color contrast between text and background.",
          "Alternative text for meaningful images.",
          "Full keyboard navigation with a clear focus indicator.",
          "Responsive layout for narrow screens and mobile devices."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Accessibility at the venue",
        "list": [
          "Step-free access at the entrance.",
          "Accessible toilets on site.",
          "A friendly team happy to help with anything you need."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Exclusions and limitations",
        "body": [
          "We make every effort to keep the site accessible and to update it regularly. Even so, some sections or content may not yet be fully accessible. We continue to improve accessibility as part of our commitment to making the site usable by everyone."
        ]
      }
    ],
